depgraph: take mergeable_nodes from the leaf frontier in _serialize_tasks

Sub-series: B (cycle search and frontier) - patch 1 of 6; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.

The frontier that _serialize_tasks already maintains returns the same nodes
in the same order as the get_nodes() scan of the whole graph.

Alone on 3.0.83: start 119.6 -> 108.6; no effect on states with a short
merge list (masks, base).
Patches 0001-0003 together, sum of six states: 447.5 -> 300.6 s (-33 %):
  start 85.8, holds 30.4, masks 59.9, py313 53.6, bdeps 40.5, policykit 30.4
Applies to upstream head unchanged.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
---
--- a/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
+++ b/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
@@ -10020,9 +10020,24 @@
                     priority_ranges.append(DepPrioritySatisfiedRange)
 
                 for local_priority_range in priority_ranges:
-                    mergeable_nodes = set(
-                        get_nodes(ignore_priority=local_priority_range.ignore_medium)
-                    )
+                    if frontier is not None:
+                        # ignore_medium is ignore_priority[MEDIUM] for both
+                        # ranges, and frontier_leaves() returns the nodes of
+                        # get_nodes() in the same order, without the scan of
+                        # the whole graph.
+                        mergeable_nodes = set(
+                            frontier_leaves(
+                                local_priority_range.ignore_priority[
+                                    local_priority_range.MEDIUM
+                                ]
+                            )
+                        )
+                    else:
+                        mergeable_nodes = set(
+                            get_nodes(
+                                ignore_priority=local_priority_range.ignore_medium
+                            )
+                        )
                     if mergeable_nodes:
                         selected_nodes, ignore_priority = find_smallest_cycle(
                             mergeable_nodes, local_priority_range
@@ -10366,7 +10381,10 @@
                 # only trigger when the graph is nearly empty and the only
                 # remaining nodes are isolated (no parents or children). Since
                 # the nodes must be isolated, ignore_priority is not needed.
-                selected_nodes = get_nodes()
+                if frontier is not None:
+                    selected_nodes = frontier_leaves(None)
+                else:
+                    selected_nodes = get_nodes()
 
             if not selected_nodes and not drop_satisfied:
                 drop_satisfied = True
